# Deny-by-default build context. Git ignore rules do NOT apply to `docker build`, so without this
# `COPY . .` would bake .git, .env files, survey_data/ (responses, sessions, uploads), exports/reports,
# overlays, reference material, local DBs/backups and caches into the image. Everything is excluded,
# then exactly what the image needs is re-included. Add a path here only if the runtime reads it.
*

# --- what `pip install .` needs to build the package
!src
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!LICENSE
!NOTICE
!MANIFEST.in
!CHANGELOG.md

# --- what the runtime serves from /app (SURVEY_DIR=surveys; the sidecar reads SURVEY_TRIGGERS_DIR)
!surveys/*.survey.json
!surveys/*.md
# file-based lifecycle state: the runtime only serves `live` surveys, and "live" is recorded here
!surveys/.registry.json
# immutable per-version snapshots: respondents mid-survey stay pinned to the version they started on
!surveys/.versions
!surveys/.versions/**
!triggers/*.json

# --- never, even inside an allowed directory (these rules come last so they win)
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
**/.DS_Store
**/*.local.md
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.db
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.sqlite-*
**/*.bak
